<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schleusingen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schleusingen is a small town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the southern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringian-forest">Thuringian Forest</a>. From the 13th century it was the main residence of the counts of Henneberg-Schleusingen, whose Bertholdsburg castle still stands. Count George Ernest founded its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">gymnasium</a> in 1577, and after the Henneberg line died out in 1583 the town passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schleusingen.jpg" alt="Schleusingen" width="299" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: own work by Geograv · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schleusingen_in_HBN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
